{"name":"Castaway Lagoon","hex":"#607374","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"castaway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cast adrift or ashore; marooned.","Shipwrecked."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shipwrecked sailor.","A discarded person or thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/castaway"},{"term":"lagoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shallow body of water separated from deeper sea by a bar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lagoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Castaway","blocks":[{"text":"A castaway is a person who is cast adrift or ashore. While the situation usually happens after a shipwreck, some people voluntarily stay behind on a desert island, either to evade captors or the world in general. A person may also be left ashore as punishment (marooned)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg/330px-Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castaway"},{"title":"Lagoon","blocks":[{"text":"A lagoon is a shallow body of water separated from a larger body of water by a narrow landform, such as a reef, a barrier island or islands, a barrier peninsula, or an isthmus. Lagoons are commonly divided into coastal lagoons and atoll lagoons. They have also been identified as occurring on mixed-sand and gravel coastlines. There is an overlap between bodies of water classified as coastal lagoons and bodies of water classified as estuaries. Lagoons are common coastal features around many parts of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/BalosLagoonCreta.jpg/330px-BalosLagoonCreta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagoon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/1280px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castaways may need to survive on a desert island.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADesertisland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Robinson Crusoe (1719) by Daniel Defoe. Illustration of Crusoe standing over Man Friday after freeing him from the cannibals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Kara-Bogaz_Gol_from_space%2C_September_1995.jpg/500px-Kara-Bogaz_Gol_from_space%2C_September_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Kara-Bogaz_Gol_from_space%2C_September_1995.jpg/500px-Kara-Bogaz_Gol_from_space%2C_September_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Garabogazköl lagoon in Turkmenistan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKara-Bogaz_Gol_from_space%2C_September_1995.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Venice_Lagoon_December_9_20